WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.450
Fear not, Mandalorian fans everyone's favorite
50-year-old infant will be on shelves in time

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.980
for Christmas, in some form or another.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.870
Disney has announced that merchandise featuring
"The Child" — or, as viewers of the Disney+

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.770
series have affectionately nicknamed it, "Baby
Yoda" — will be on sale in the weeks leading

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:17.900
up to Christmas.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.769
According to CNBC, the merch will include
"apparel and accessories," and while no specific

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:26.900
mention was made of plush toys… we simply
can't imagine that there won't be Baby Yoda

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.330
plush toys sitting under Christmas trees this
year, even if they might hit shelves a little

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.990
later in the holiday season.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:37.350
In case you've been hiding under a rock since
The Mandalorian's debut, the Star Wars series

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:41.570
focuses on the titular bounty hunter, who
is tasked with bringing in a target that has

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:45.940
proven ridiculously difficult for members
of his nefarious Guild to get their scummy

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.940
hands on.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.030
Said target is located under heavily armed
guard at a remote fortress on the harsh desert

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:56.590
planet of Arvala-7, and with the help of a
bounty hunting droid, IG-11, the Mandalorian

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.870
is able to nab it.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:02.710
To his surprise, the target is a half-century
old, infant member of the same unnamed race

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:04.650
as the iconic Jedi Master Yoda.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:09.509
Rather than allow IG-11 to terminate it, the
Mandalorian dispatches the droid — setting

00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:12.990
off one of the oddest interplanetary buddy
adventures of all time.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:17.250
The silent, contemplative, Force-sensitive
"Child" instantly captured the hearts and

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.659
minds of viewers, because it is — in a word
— adorable.

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:25.520
Its reveal at the conclusion of The Mandalorian's
debut episode was a heck of a surprise, so

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.409
it's no wonder that merch centered around
the floppy-eared tot wasn't made available

00:01:29.409 --> 00:01:30.899
prior to its premiere.

00:01:30.899 --> 00:01:34.710
But there's no way Disney didn't know the
extent to which the character would captivate

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:38.759
the series' viewers, so it seems pretty likely
that the House of Mouse will do its best to

00:01:38.759 --> 00:01:46.340
make sure that under every household's tree,
a Baby Yoda there will be.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:51.109
"This is what was causing all the fuss?"

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:55.420
Of course, Hasbro — which holds the license
to produce Star Wars toys — has had no comment

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.820
on when actual plush toys will be available.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.920
In the informed opinion of one industry insider,
though, failing to exploit that market would

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.450
be akin to tearing up a license to print money.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:08.520
Marissa DiBartolo, Editor-in-Chief of The
Toy Insider, told MarketWatch:

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.830
"As long as the merch hits before the holidays,
it's going to be a huge success.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:16.820
If it drops before Black Friday, which we
expect it will, I guarantee it'll be gone

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:17.820
in an instant.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.350
'Baby Yoda' will be the Tickle Me Elmo of
2019 just grab yours before it ends up on

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.350
eBay."

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:28.110
"No wonder he's laughing — all the way to
the bank — because North America has been

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:30.790
gripped by Tickle Me Elmo hysteria."

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:31.790
"Oh boy!

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:32.790
That tickles!"

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:36.920
It stands to reason that within a few months
at the most, you'll be able to pick up Baby

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:42.250
Yoda toys, mugs, hats, and probably anything
else you could conceive of at retail outlets

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:45.590
from department stores all the way down to
your local gas station.

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:48.950
In order to score some merch in time for the
holiday, though, you'll have to know where

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:49.950
to look.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.680
In the weeks leading up to Christmas, you
may want to check department stores Target,

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:59.410
Kohl's, and Macy's, as well as specialty retailers
Zazzle, Hot Topic, and Box Lunch.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:03.840
Also, some products will be available at the
Disney Store, on the website ShopDisney.com,

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.790
and at Disney Parks.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:09.900
At this point, it's being reported that consumers
will be able to pre-order toys — including

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.650
those of the plush variety — over the coming
weeks.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.960
It's unclear exactly what type of merchandise
is expected to ship in the coming weeks, but

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.370
again, we'd be shocked if Disney's goal wasn't
to get a plush Baby Yoda into the hands of

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:23.460
everybody who wants one by Christmas.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:27.820
Now, there's always the chance that the Tickle
Me Elmo comparison could prove to be apt,

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:32.450
and that the demand for Baby Yoda toys over
the next month could far exceed the supply.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:37.260
Given the cuddly critter's explosive popularity,
in fact, we find this to be pretty likely

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.540
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:42.960
Plus, even more Looper videos about Star Wars
are coming soon.

